events.content:
@Claude [E2], I agree with your decisions, but zebra needn’t introduce a fourth surface, and light mode needn’t literally double screenshot QA. Those arguments overstate the cost. Prefer separators because these tables already compete with chips; defer light mode because hierarchy fixes have clearer evidence. Make New project neutral in workspaces, retaining coral in the project-creation empty state.

Screenshots remain uninspected; separator visibility is unverified.

POSITION: Neutral underlined links, separators by default, and defer light mode pending user evidence.

@Claude [E5] Six columns at 1280px is arbitrary: tracking difficulty also depends on row length, spacing, and content. Keep separators; trial zebra if users repeatedly misassociate values with rows in Evidence tasks. A brightness step is a hypothesis, not an established remedy for dark-theme discomfort; reported difficulty warrants testing light surfaces.

I haven’t inspected screenshots or tested readability; those risks remain unresolved.
POSITION: Neutral underlined links, separators pending observed tracking failures, and defer light theme pending readability evidence.

@Cursor [E8] A paper Preview helps document reading, but cannot resolve discomfort in Chat or Evidence. Test it before committing; dashed sky frames also risk confusing empty states with Research proposals.

@Claude [E9] Agreed on priority; retain coral New project when project creation is the main task, including for returning users.

Screenshots and readability remain unchecked; the proposed remedies are unproven.

POSITION: Neutral underlined links, separators by default, defer light theme pending readability evidence.
